43327121\">https://x.com/theauroraguy/status/1763297989043327121</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1763298968065171941</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1763298968065171941\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-29T20:23:29Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1763326891522658717":{"a":"<p>That looks quite practical, really, and something that would get your murdered by some guy in a Dodge Ram in the USA. I mean, hell, that&#x27;s what we had as teens before we could drive. Back before Dodge Rams were 19 ft tall and had 3 ft diameter tires. <a href=\"https://t.co/7mHtlrKUfQ\">t.co/7mHtlrKUfQ</a></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1763326891522658717</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1763326891522658717\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-29T22:14:26Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1763327710112448975":{"a":"<p>Hehe, that&#x27;s the dumbest and most brilliant (literally) thing I have seen all day. Man that dish could destroy an entire town if left unattended for even a minute. We had one like that in HighSchool Physics and it damn near set a car on fire when the teacher walked away for 5 min <a href=\"https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/1763009023434277131\">Tweet by @BrianRoemmele</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/1763009023434277131\">https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/1763009023434277131</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1763327710112448975</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1763327710112448975\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-29T22:17:41Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1763328627952005612":{"a":"<p>Title companies fascinate me because they just stop when they run out of chain of documents. I&#x27;m like, &quot;OK but who did the first guy to purchase a deed to the land buy the land from? I&#x27;ll sit here while you check. I have all of, what you call, eternity for you to figure it out.&quot; <a href=\"https://x.com/brettachapman/status/1763004485389946970\">Tweet by @brettachapman</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/brettachapman/status/1763004485389946970\">https://x.com/brettachapman/status/1763004485389946970</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1763328627952005612</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1763328627952005612\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-29T22:21:20Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1763331583547756983":{"a":"<p>@LandOfHistory @brettachapman I have to wonder if anything interesting is living deep inside the Indiana State Archives. My Norris family cemetery was destroyed they claim because a farmer was mad it was in his corn field. I don&#x27;t think that&#x27;s true. Mormons documented the grave markers before it was…</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1763174450818580831\">https://x.com/i/status/1763174450818580831</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/LandOfHistory/status/1763174450818580831\">https://x.com/LandOfHistory/status/1763174450818580831</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1763331583547756983</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1763331583547756983\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-29T22:33:05Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1763332823870742701":{"a":"<p>Especially wh